<title>USA: AFTER THE BELL - Sun Micro off, Amgen up.</title>
<headline>AFTER THE BELL - Sun Micro off, Amgen up.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Sun Microsystems Inc fell 4-1/2 to 65-1/2, whiles shares of Amgen Inc rose 1-5/8 to 61-1/4 after hours Tuesday, traders said.</p>
<p>After the market closed, Sun Micro reported earnings for the first quarter ended September 29 of $0.63 a share, compared to $0.42 a share the previous first quarter.</p>
<p>Amgen reported third quarter earnings of $0.64 a share versus $0.52 a share.  </p>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said Tuesday that Equity Inns Inc, Gaylord Entertainment Co, BT Office Products International Inc, and Sport Supply Group Inc were unavailable for after-hours trade for news.</p>
<p>The NYSE said that session one volume was 98,300 shares, compared to 9,600 shares Monday. There was no activity in session two Tuesday or Monday.</p>
<p>The American Stock Exchange said there was no after-hours activity.</p>
</text>
